---
title: Develop
description: The Light, Curve, Color, Effects, Detail, Optics and Geometry panels — the global adjustments Latent applies to a frame.
---

The Edit rail on the right holds the global adjustments: everything that applies to the whole
frame, as opposed to the local work described in [Masks & layers](/docs/latent/masks). Above it
sit the **Histogram** and the **Info** panel, which reads the frame's own metadata — camera, lens,
exposure, capture time, dimensions, rating, flag, folder, sidecar state and a content hash.

Each panel has a reset control, and a dot marks panels you have actually touched.

## Light

The tonal foundation, in stops and in points:

- **Exposure**, in EV
- **Contrast**
- **Highlights** and **Shadows** — recover the ends of the range
- **Whites** and **Blacks** — set where the range clips

The histogram updates as you move them, so you can see what a recovery actually bought you.

## Curve

Beneath Light is the tone curve, in two forms. **Parametric** gives you banded controls —
highlights, lights and the bands below them — which move the curve without letting you tear it.
The channel dots beside it switch between the composite curve and the individual **R**, **G** and
**B** channels, for colour work you cannot do with a saturation slider. The readout under the
grid reports the mapping at the point you are dragging, as input → output.

## Color

White balance and saturation:

- **Mode** — how the temperature control is interpreted, relative or as an absolute value
- **Temperature**, in kelvin, and **Tint**
- **Vibrance** and **Saturation**

Below them, the **Color Mixer** works per colour range rather than globally, with **Hue**,
**Saturation** and **Luminance** tabs — the way to lift one colour in a frame without dragging
every other one with it.

## Effects, Detail, Optics, Geometry

The remaining panels hold the finishing work: **Effects** for treatments applied over the graded
image, **Detail** for sharpening and noise, and **Optics** for lens corrections.

**Geometry** is crop and perspective. The crop is expressed as **Left**, **Top**, **Right** and
**Bottom** edges in normalised coordinates, so the numbers mean the same thing whatever the
frame's resolution. **Straighten** and **Rotate** are in degrees, there are horizontal and
vertical flips, and the perspective controls correct converging verticals and horizontals.

## Nothing is baked in

Every panel writes into the frame's edit stack rather than into the image. Adjustments can be
reset individually, reordered, or walked back through the [history](/docs/latent/presets); the
RAW file itself is never rewritten. See [Files & sidecars](/docs/latent/files).
